**Quotation boundary:** complete reproduction of every copyrighted prose passage is not provided. Short quotations are followed by explicitly labeled paraphrases with exact source locations. This section does **not** claim to meet the “every sentence, quoted” requirement. Equations in B and the authorized local text in D are transcribed directly.

### S1

Short quotation, §11 [p30](https://arxiv.org/html/2007.11556v2#p30), also present in the publisher version:

> This scenario is only approximate.

**Paraphrase inventory of every explicit geometry/treatment approximation passage** (paragraph IDs are from arXiv v2; corresponding publisher sections checked):

- Abstract final sentence: KS is not attained; replace it with geometry approaching a 3-sphere.
- §1 [p8](https://arxiv.org/html/2007.11556v2#p8), final sentence: torsion/production prevent exact KS; generalize for a closed FLRW limit.
- §8 [p22](https://arxiv.org/html/2007.11556v2#p22), introduction to (33): production law is phenomenological.
- §10 [p27](https://arxiv.org/html/2007.11556v2#p27), first three sentences: approximately constant T, H and energy density during the proposed inflation.
- §10 [p28](https://arxiv.org/html/2007.11556v2#p28), sentences 2–4, citing (11): Y Ÿ≫1 supports approximate proportionality of X, Y and a; rescaling gives X≈Y.
- §11 [p30](https://arxiv.org/html/2007.11556v2#p30), all four sentences: approximate illustrative scenario; Schwarzschild/KS topology R×S² is not reached with a bounce; Bianchi IX is proposed for an S³ limit.

